    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5519168/assistant-professor-business-administration-management": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Business Administration/Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Business Administration/Management Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00527 Division Academic Affairs Department Business/Accounting/Economics Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of Management. We seek candidates who will contribute to the department’s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: The candidate is expected to excel in the areas of teaching, scholarship, research and service related to Otterbein’s bachelor’s degree in Business Administration and Management. Teaching responsibilities will be primarily in Principles of Management (Writing Intensive), Personnel/Human Resource Management, Leadership and Culture, Training and Development, and Business and Society. Research responsibilities include publishing in peer-reviewed journals and presenting research at peer-reviewed conferences in business administration, management, or related fields. Faculty members are also expected to be involved in professional and community activities for the purposes of scholarship, professional development, student advising and mentorship, and service. COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor (terminal degree) - $71,500 (plus full University benefits). If initial appointment is at the rank of Instructor - $62,000 (plus full University benefits). WHEN: This appointment will begin August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: A PhD or DBA in a business discipline from an Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) accredited university with a specialization in Management is required. Candidates who are ABD will be considered if they are within one year of completing their doctoral degree. Effective teaching experience at the baccalaureate level and demonstrated record of scholarship is also required. The ideal candidate must possess superior communication, leadership and organization skills, and an ability to work effectively with students, faculty and staff from diverse communities and cultures. This is a tenure-track position with commensurate expectations for teaching, scholarship, and service. Candidates who have not completed their terminal degree at the time of appointment will be appointed at the rank of instructor on a non-tenure track basis. APPLICATION: To apply: submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, contact information for three references, research statement, and a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein’s belonging plan? Preference given to applicants who submit materials by November 19, 2026. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION DEPARTMENT: The Department of Business, Accounting & Economics is composed of 9 full-time faculty and 7 part-time faculty. Majors offered: a B.S. in Accounting, Business Administration & Management, Business Analytics, Finance and Marketing as well as a B.A. in Economics (Changing to Environmental Economics and Sustainability in July 2027). Minors offered: Accounting, Business Administration, Economics, International Business & Management, Finance, Marketing, Marketing Analytics. The department is dedicated to providing a personalized education of distinction that leads our graduates to inquiring, ethical, humane, and productive lives as global citizens. The faculty is focused on action-oriented learning by integrating classroom knowledge with practice through internships, research, service projects, study abroad, participation in professional associations, and networking with employers, faculty, alumni, community leaders, and recruiters. To learn about all the programs offered in the Department of Business, Accounting & Economics, please visit https://www.otterbein.edu/business-accounting-economics/. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY : Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio’s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein has been selected as one of 23 universities across the US and the first in Ohio to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. Otterbein University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is a member of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. For more than a decade, Otterbein has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for its academic quality. In the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Otterbein ranked #12 among 160 Regional Universities in the Midwest. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine’s Top 100 list of Americas’ “Best Places to Live” and recognized as one of Forbes “America’s Friendliest Towns.” Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital; a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5524064/assistant-professor-criminology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Criminology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Criminology Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00528 Division Academic Affairs Department Sociology Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University, a comprehensive liberal arts institution, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Criminology . RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: Full-time tenure-track faculty members teach seven, three-credit-hour courses per academic year. In addition to departmental courses, this faculty member will have the opportunity to teach in the general education program. Faculty are also required to have an active research agenda, provide service to the department and university, and advise students in the departmental majors and minors. WHEN: This appointment begins in August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS PhD (assistant professor) in Sociology (with a specialization in criminology) or Criminology at the time of appointment is required. Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence, have an active program of scholarship that can involve undergraduates, and be interested in teaching, advising, and mentoring students from diverse backgrounds. Preference will be given to candidates with the ability to incorporate a critical criminology and social justice focus into their pedagogy, teaching, and advising. In addition to teaching Introduction to Sociology, the preferred candidate will be interested in and able to teach sociology of corrections, research methods, criminological theory, gender and/or race and ethnic studies, in addition to courses in the candidate’s area of specialty. Experience with internships or other experiential learning pedagogies would be appreciated. APPLICATION : Apply through NeoeD and attach (1) a cover letter; (2) your curriculum vitae; (3) your teaching philosophy (not more than 3 pages); and (4) a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein’s Belonging Plan? Review of applications begins November 20, 2026. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor - $62,226 (plus full University benefits). DEPARTMENT : The Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies at Otterbein University currently has two full-time faculty and committed and talented part-time faculty serving roughly 80 majors, along with our general education programs and students in Race and Ethnic Studies, Public Health Education, Legal Studies, Sustainability Studies, and Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies. We offer a BA in Sociology, a BA in Criminology & Justice Studies, and minors in Sociology, Criminology & Justice Studies, and Justice Studies. We offer students a multi-level understanding of global connections and social forces acting on interaction, identities, social groups, organizations, communities, and nations. We foster the knowledge and skills necessary to effectively work for justice in institutions, workplaces, and as engaged citizens. Department faculty and students create scholarship and applied learning opportunities in preparation for diverse careers and graduate education in sociology, criminology, and related fields such as social work, human and community services, public policy, the law, and justice related fields. To learn more about the Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies, visit https://www.otterbein.edu/sociology-criminology-justice-studies/. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY : Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio’s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein is the first university in Ohio to be selected by the American Association of Colleges and Universities to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine’s Top 100 list of Americas’ “Best Places to Live” and recognized as one of Forbes “America’s Friendliest Towns.” Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital, a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5524117/assistant-professor-philosophy-religion": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Philosophy & Religion",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Philosophy & Religion Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00529 Division Academic Affairs Department Religion & Philosophy Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of Philosophy & Religion. We invite applications from philosophers, scholars of religion, and interdisciplinary teacher-scholars with interests in philosophical ethics, and Buddhism, Hinduism, or other religious traditions of Asia. We seek candidates who will contribute to the department’s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES : Teaching load is 3 - 4 which includes teaching courses in Applied and Theoretical Ethics, Religions of India, Buddhism, and other general education courses on topics in Asian philosophical and religious traditions. Candidates should be committed to increasing the diversity of our curriculum and student body. We seek candidates with evidence of success teaching undergraduates, a commitment to recruiting and retaining majors and minors in our department, a commitment to student-centered undergraduate teaching, and the ability to excite students about the study of philosophy and religion. Faculty members are also expected to be involved in professional and community activities for the purposes of scholarship, professional development, student advising and mentorship, and service. New faculty are eligible for a reduced instructional workload during their first year to establish a research program, along with opportunities for ongoing professional development funding and support from our Center for Teaching and Learning. WHEN : This appointment will begin August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. in a relevant field of study by the start of appointment. Applicants should have an interest in decolonizing approaches to the study of religion and philosophy and a commitment to social justice-oriented approaches in the classroom. We seek applicants who will complement the existing strengths of our department in analytic philosophy and the Abrahamic religious traditions and who can teach courses in ethics as well as in Asian religious traditions. We are particularly interested in a teacher-scholar who takes a cultural approach to the study of the religions and philosophical traditions of Asia with teaching expertise that emphasizes such areas as the critical study of race, gender, sexuality, and social location. APPLICATION : Submit cover letter, curriculum vitae, three references - including contact information, and a teaching portfolio ( including a teaching statement, areas of teaching interest, syllabi and teaching evaluations ). As to syllabi, please include syllabi for a course in philosophical ethics as well as a course focusing on an Asian religious tradition, suitable for introductory students. Additionally, a diversity statement is also required, consisting of no more than one single-spaced page, addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Priority will be given to applications received by November 20, 2026. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION DEPARTMENT: The Department is composed of three full-time faculty. One of the full-time faculty is trained in analytic philosophy, the second in religious studies, focusing on Christianity, Islam, and Judaism. The successful applicant for this position will fill the third full-time faculty slot. The Department services one major in Philosophy and Religion and two minors (one in Religion, and one in Philosophy). The bulk of our teaching is to general education students (through the Integrative Studies Program) but we also are connected to the Legal Studies Minor, the Environmental and Sustainability Studies Major, the Honors Program, and the minor in Race and Ethnic Studies. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY : Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio’s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein has been selected as one of 23 universities across the US and the first in Ohio to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. Otterbein University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is a member of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. For more than a decade, Otterbein has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for its academic quality. In the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Otterbein ranked #12 among 160 Regional Universities in the Midwest. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine’s Top 100 list of Americas’ “Best Places to Live” and recognized as one of Forbes “America’s Friendliest Towns.” Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital; a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5524139/assistant-professor-communication-studies": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Communication Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Communication Studies Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00530 Division Academic Affairs Department Communication Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of Communication Studies. We seek candidates who will contribute to the department’s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: The Assistant Professor will teach seven courses each year in Communication, advise students, and maintain a program of scholarship and service. The Assistant Professor will also play a key role in maintaining and supporting Otterbein’s award-winning speech and debate team, which comprises part of the teaching load. Courses will be selected from Argumentation, Public Speaking, Communicating with Audiences and Professional and Persuasive Writing. Additional opportunities exist to teach in specific areas of interest, as well as in the Freshman Year Seminar, Integrative Studies and Senior Year Experience programs. Faculty members are also expected to be involved in professional and community activities for the purposes of scholarship, professional development, student advising and mentorship, and service. WHEN : This appointment will begin August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. in Speech Communication, Communication Studies, Rhetoric OR a J.D. with a background in speech and debate required for tenure-track appointment; experience in competitive speech and debate required; desire to work with and mentor students; teaching experience required. The ideal candidate will have experience with and enthusiasm for the student speech and debate team, prior teaching experience in a liberal arts setting, an established program of scholarship, and a commitment to excellence in teaching. The candidate must also possess superior communication, leadership, and organizational skills, as well as the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff from diverse communities and cultures. This tenure-track position carries commensurate expectations for teaching, scholarship, and service. APPLICATION : To apply: submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, contact information for three references, research statement, and a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein’s belonging plan? Preference given to applicants who submit materials by November 25. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor (terminal degree) - $62,226 (plus full University benefits). DEPARTMENT: The Department of Communication houses programs in communication studies, journalism and media communication, health communication and public relations. The department supports robust student co-curricular activities, which have resulted in speech and debate championships, PRSSA recognition and awards for journalism and audio/video production. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSIT Y : Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio’s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein has been selected as one of 23 universities across the US and the first in Ohio to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. Otterbein University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is a member of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. For more than a decade, Otterbein has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for its academic quality. In the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Otterbein ranked #12 among 160 Regional Universities in the Midwest. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine’s Top 100 list of Americas’ “Best Places to Live” and recognized as one of Forbes “America’s Friendliest Towns.” Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital; a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5524803/assistant-professor-sport-management": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Sport Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Sport Management Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00532 Division Academic Affairs Department Health & Sport Sciences Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University, a comprehensive liberal arts institution, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Sports Management . RESPONSIBILITIES We are seeking an innovative and collaborative colleague for this full time, tenure-track position with commensurate expectations for teaching, scholarship, and service. Candidates will teach 9-12 credit hours per semester. Courses taught will include: Professional Perspectives in Sport Management (i.e., introductory course); Practicum in Sport Management (i.e., career development and field experience); Sport Finance and Economics; and oversight of required student internship program. Additional courses that may be taught will include: Sport Marketing; Sport Facility and Design; and/or contributions to the University’s general education program or elective course development. The candidate should have a commitment to teaching in a comprehensive liberal arts-based institution along with a commitment to service-based activities to the department, University, community, and profession. In addition to teaching and service, candidates must also be able to maintain an active research agenda and serve as an academic advisor and mentor to a diverse sport management undergraduate student population. Other assignments may include assisting with the Sport Management Club and/or other student groups and activities on campus. WHEN: This appointment begins in August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have an earned doctorate in Sport Management or Sport Management-related field. One to three years of college teaching required (more than three years preferred) with experience using technology as well as a variety of instructional strategies. Experience with course development preferred. The ideal candidate must possess superior communication, leadership and organizational skills, and an ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff from diverse communities and cultures. In addition, candidates must be able to maintain an active research agenda, engage in professional and university services activities, serve as an academic advisor, and successfully teach 9-12 credit hours per semester. APPLICATION: Apply through Neoed and please submit: (1) cover letter of interest, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy, (4) a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein’s Belonging Plan? and (5) a statement of research agenda/interests, and (6) three current professional references. Review of applications will begin November 6, 2026 . Finalists for the position will be asked to submit official transcripts for their highest degree earned. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor - $71,500 (plus full University benefits). OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio’s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein is the first university in Ohio to be selected by the American Association of Colleges and Universities to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE: Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine’s Top 100 list of Americas’ “Best Places to Live” and recognized as one of Forbes “America’s Friendliest Towns.” Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital, a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein considers diversity and inclusion as integral parts of the University’s achievement of excellence. We welcome applications from candidates from groups that have been historically underrepresented in higher education. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5528981/assistant-professor-american-history": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, American History",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, American History Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00534 Division Academic Affairs Department History & Political Science Opening Date 10/26/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of American History. We seek candidates who will contribute to the department’s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: The Assistant Professor will teach lower- and upper-division topical courses in the History major, teach the department’s historical research methods course in rotation with other departmental faculty, and contribute sections of a US History course with a global focus to Otterbein University’s Integrated Studies Program. The faculty member in this position may also teach courses in the Honors Program, the First-Year Experience (FYE) Program, and the Senior Year Experience (SYE) Program in accordance with candidate preference and with institutional needs. Faculty members are also expected to be involved in professional and community activities for the purposes of scholarship, professional development, student advising and mentorship, and service. COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor (terminal degree) - $62,226 (plus full University benefits). WHEN: This appointment will begin August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. in American History is required. ABD applicants will be considered but need to have completed their degree requirements by position start date. We seek an outstanding applicant with an active research agenda and a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching in a liberal arts context. The successful candidate will be committed to fostering undergraduate research, to effective teaching from an interdisciplinary and multi-cultural perspective, and to service in the department and University. We seek a specialist in modern American political, social, or cultural history, with a temporal focus no earlier than the 19 th century. Candidates with subfields in women and gender and/or race and ethnic studies are especially welcome to apply, as are those with an ability to teach from a global or comparative perspective. The candidate must also possess superior communication, leadership, and organizational skills, as well as the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff from diverse communities and cultures. This tenure-track position carries commensurate expectations for teaching, scholarship, and service. APPLICATION: To apply: submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, contact information for three references, research statement, and a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein’s belonging plan? Preference given to applicants who submit materials by December 1. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION DEPARTMENT: The Department of History, Political Science, Languages and Cultures centers around the academic study of history, politics, law, cultures, languages, and global relations. Each of our department’s four majors — History, Political Science, Global Studies, and Spanish and Latin American Studies — includes a global focus that allows students to study areas beyond U.S. borders and to learn about interconnections between the United States and other regions. We offer opportunities for immersive language learning, study abroad, co-curricular international travel, service learning, internships, and undergraduate research. We emphasize the development of critical thinking, writing, and communication skills to prepare students for a wide variety of careers, graduate and law school, and lifelong learning. The department connects to and supports the University’s commitment to Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging through promoting student understanding of the richness and diversity of human experience across time and across the globe. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY : Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio’s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein has been selected as one of 23 universities across the US and the first in Ohio to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. Otterbein University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is a member of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. For more than a decade, Otterbein has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for its academic quality. In the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Otterbein ranked #12 among 160 Regional Universities in the Midwest. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine’s Top 100 list of Americas’ “Best Places to Live” and recognized as one of Forbes “America’s Friendliest Towns.” Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital; a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"
